heckpointRestore:`Back to checkpoint`,checkpointClear:`Remove checkpoint`,timeLabel:`TIME`,resultOrdinal:e=>`RUN #${e}`,resultPlace:(e,t)=>`PLACE ${e}/${t}`,resultShort:(e,t)=>`${e}/${t}`,veilTitle:`Still there?`,veilText:`The clock is stopped. Tap to get back to the board.`,menuButton:`Pause menu`,pauseTitle:`Paused`,pauseState:`CLOCK STOPPED`,pauseResume:`Resume`,pauseReset:`Clear the board`,pauseHelp:`How to play`,pauseCopy:`Copy the board id`,pauseCopyDone:`Your friend pastes this id into “Open a board by id” and gets the same board.`,pauseCopyFailed:`Copying failed — select the id and copy it by hand.`,pauseExit:`Exit to the menu`,resetTitle:`Clear the board?`,resetText:`The tiles and the walls come off. The clock does not go back to zero — it carries on from the same number.`,resetConfirm:`Clear`,resetCancel:`Cancel`,helpTitle:`How to play`,helpIntro:`A domino tile is two halves with numbers on them. Break the whole board into tiles: every pair of numbers turns up in the set exactly once.`,helpSwipe:`Drag your finger from a square to the one next to it and a tile lands along the way. Keep the finger down and one drag lays a whole chain.`,helpTap:`Or tap two neighbouring squares: the first waits for a partner, the second lays the tile. A tap right on the seam between them lays it at once.`,helpRemove:`A tile in the wrong place? Tap it and it comes apart again.`,helpDuplicate:`If that tile is already on the board, both of them turn red and its cell in the table shows a red cross. No harm done — one of the two has to move.`,helpMatrix:`The table beside the board is the whole set: a row and a column are the two halves of a tile. A filled cell means that tile is already on the board.`,helpModes:`The switch next to the table: tiles or walls. It decides what a tap on the board does.`,helpWalls:`A wall is a mark on the border between two squares: no tile gets through here. Tap near that edge of a square to put a wall up, tap again to take it down. Keep the finger down and drag it along the border: the walls go up one after another. The board itself does not change.`,helpAuto:`When walls have closed every border of two neighbouring squares but the one they share, the tile lands on its own: it cannot be anything else.`,helpCheckpoint:`Below them are the three checkpoint buttons. The flag remembers the whole board, the arrow brings it back to what was remembered, the crossed-out flag drops the mark. You can come back as often as you like, but the clock never rewinds: it keeps running.`,helpShow:`Show me`,helpClose:`Got it`,lessonSteps:{swipeFirst:`Drag from one cell to the next — a tile lands along the way.`,removeBone:`Tap a tile and it comes apart.`,tapPair:`Tap a cell, then its neighbour — same tile, no dragging.`,swipeChain:`Keep your finger down — one move lays a whole chain.`,seamTap:`A tap right on the seam between two cells places a tile at once.`},lessonNotices:{duplicateSeen:`That tile is already down — both are red. Tap either one to remove it.`,matrixFilled:`The table beside the board is the whole set. A filled cell means the tile is down.`,offerWalls:`A wall marks “no tile crosses here” and changes nothing on the board. See what it is for?`,offerCheckpoint:`That branch did not work out, and taking it apart one tile at a time is slow. See the shortcut?`},lessonSkip:`Skip`,lessonGot:`Got it`,lessonNo:`No thanks`,sceneTexts:{wallsTitle:`Why walls`,wallsMode:`The switch next to the table — press “Walls” on it.`,wallsFirst:`The 2-3 tile is already down, and there is no second one. So it cannot be here — drag along this border.`,wallsSecond:`Same on the right: the 0-2 tile is down too. Cut that border off as well.`,wallsPlace:`One free neighbour is left. Switch back to tiles and place the tile upwards — it cannot be anything else.`,wallsDone:`A wall changes nothing on the board. It remembers for you: what is ruled out stays visible instead of living in your head.`,checkpointTitle:`Why checkpoints`,checkpointFork:`Two ways from here — right and down, both tiles free. Nothing tells them apart, so plant a flag before you try.`,checkpointTry:`Try the right one: tile 1-4.`,checkpointForced:`Forced from here — this cell has one neighbour left.`,checkpointClash:`And the pocket above. Watch what happens.`,checkpointBack:`Red means the branch did not work out. Return the board to the flag — one press instead of three removals.`,checkpointRight:`Now the other way: the tile downwards.`,checkpointDone:`The flag stays until you clear it, and you can return as often as you like. Time does not rewind though — the clock keeps running.`},sceneClose:`Close`,sceneDone:`Done`,lessonLabel:`Tutorial`,resumeTitle:`A game is unfinished`,resumeText:e=>`It is waiting here: ${e}. Start a new level and it is gone.`,resumeContinue:`Back to that game`,resumeRestart:`Start the new level`,resumeCancel:`Cancel`,resumeTextFree:e=>`It is waiting here: ${e}. Opening another board drops it.`,resumeRestartFree:`Open the new board`,chaptersTitle:`Levels`,chaptersCount:(e,t)=>`${e}/${t}`,chaptersClose:`Close`,levelDone:`solved`,levelOpen:`open`,levelLocked:`locked`,winTitle:`Full set!`,winOrdinalLabel:`RUN`,winOrdinal:e=>`#${e}`,placePending:`counting your place`,placeMissing:`—`,winPlaceLabel:`PLACE`,winPlace:(e,t)=>`${e}/${t}`,winContinue:`Continue`,winToBuilder:`Back to the generator`,winToMenu:`Back to the menu`,finaleTitle:`You finished the game`,finaleText:`Every board is solved. Thanks for playing.`,finaleButton:`Pick a level`,menuTitle:`Boneset`,menuStart:`Start`,menuResume:`Continue`,menuGenerate:`Generate a level`,menuCampaign:`Campaign`,menuCampaignCount:(e,t)=>`${e}/${t}`,menuBuilder:`Level generator`,menuHistory:`History`,menuHistoryCount:e=>`${e} board${e===1?``:`s`}`,menuChallenges:`Challenges`,menuChallengeDone:`solved`,menuChallengeLeft:(e,t,n)=>e===0?`${p(t)}:${p(n)}`:e<10?`${e}d ${p(t)}h`:`${e}d`,menuSound:`Sound`,menuSoundOn:`Sound is on`,menuSoundOff:`Sound is off`,menuLanguage:`Language`,menuLanguageClo